<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50584" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vernŭla</span></b> , ae, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>comm. dim.</i>
			[verna], <i>a little</i> or <i>young
				home-born slave</i> (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Juv. 10,
				117</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Prov. 1, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 22,
				17, 20, § 44</span></i>; <i><span class="en">App. M. 4,
				p. 153, 25 al.</span></i>— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, adj.: = vernaculus.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Jocular</i>, <i>pert</i>, <i>coarse</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbanitas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 24</span></i>
			 (al. vernacula).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Native</i>, <i>indigenous</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lupus Tiberinus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					5, 105</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">libelli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					5, 18, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
